@up UP link: UP is India's **most populous state** (19.98 crore in 2011; about **23-24 crore** projected for 2026), larger than every country except China, India, the USA and Indonesia. **Allahabad (Prayagraj)** is its most populous district (59.5 lakh), followed by **Moradabad, Ghaziabad and Azamgarh**; **Mahoba** is the least populous. UP's growth is driven by **better health and disease control** with still-high fertility.

@trap
**Malthus: population geometric, food arithmetic.** **Optimum population: Cannan; DTT: Thompson; social maladjustment: Henry George.** **First census 1872 (Mayo); regular 1881 (Ripon).** **Census 2011 slogan: Our Census, Our Future.** **Census 2027 = 16th, digital, with caste.** **1921 = Great Divide (only fall).** **Highest decadal growth 1961-71; highest exponential 1971-81; lowest 2001-11 (17.7%).** **UP 16.5% of India.** **Maharashtra 2nd in population, 3rd in area.** **Nagaland: highest growth 1991-2001, only fall 2001-11.**
@end

